    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0573" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg557"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.61351/6–148</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Senator Eugene D.
                        Millikin </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d414-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-02">June 2, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Senator Millikin</hi>: Reference is again
                    made to your letter of April 20, 1948<anchor n="2" xml:id="d414-f2"/>,
                    requesting the State Department’s comments on S. 2511, a bill “Repealing section
                    202 (<hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>) of the Sugar Act of 1948.”</p>
                <p>In view of the fact that the intent of this section of the Act has been widely
                    misunderstood and that circumstances under which the use of this section might
                    be considered desirable now appear remote, the Department perceives no objection
                    to its repeal.</p>
                <p>The Department has been informed by the Bureau of the Budget that there is no
                    objection to the submission of this report.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles</hi> E. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Bohlen</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Counselor</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d414-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d414-f1-content">
